From b1c9c257887cb348c3c8e4791ec0c15f40163a9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:18:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] ONSITE-1: read-only on-site prep -- drive torque-limit
 read-back (60E0h/60E1h) and an ioweb_probe DI watch mode for mapping the
 safety doors
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Weekend plan, machine share (laptop agreed 20260926): measure read-only whether the SGDXS/SGDXW drives support the torque-limit
objects that kCmdAxTorqueLimitSet writes, and find which 1203 input each safety door is wired to (plan "20260924 下午新發現").
Nothing here writes to the card; neither tool has been run on the card yet (that is the on-site session).
- Monitor (EastSun's module, line counts unchanged): the kCfgDrive block also reads 60E0h/60E1h (U16, +0x800 for axis B) with the
  already-allowed Acm_DevReadSDOData, Yield_() after each, same due/throttle rules; Pci1203AxisSample trqLimVal/Valid/Ret/RetText
  (ok / readFailed + vendor code and text / notRead); a failed read is not retried and does not set cfgBad (like homeVal[4]/[5]).
  Allowlist prose names the two objects; kCmdAxTorqueLimitSet now marks kCfgDrive due after it is issued so the read-back refreshes.
- Tags: pci1203.axN.trqLim.pos/.neg (0.1 %, null unless read OK), .posRead/.negRead (status), .posRet/.negRet (vendor code).
- tools/ioweb_probe: `ioweb_probe <outDir> <seconds> watch` prints every DI bit change with ring/station/chan/bit and every
  IO_Table row the web page would read there (ISABase 3, IP=station, Port=chan*8+bit, Enable=0 rows included), "(no ePCI1203 row)"
  otherwise, legacy "Port=byte, Bit=bit" rows separately as Bit-column candidates, and at start the door rows that are not on the
  1203 table yet; appends watch_di_changes.csv. Both modes print the torque-limit answer right after the first successful Poll and
  write card_axes.csv at once (+8 columns at the end); Ctrl+C / close only sets a flag, the main thread writes the outputs and
  closes the monitor. Pure logic in tools/ioweb_watch.h.
Tests: new IoWatch_HT9050 (row-by-row agreement with ChanIoPoints ResolveIoPoint on machines/HT9050/IO_Table.csv: 229 input rows;
legacy rows; door rows off the 1203), WB_Tags pins the new tag names (null with no monitor), Pci1203Pure, IoPoints_HT9050 --
pass on build_integ_ship_x86 (WinLibs) and build_integ_ora_ship_x86 (MinGW.org 6.3.0); production_audit 0 changes around every
ctest; pci1203_readonly_gate PASS (30 calls, same set); control gate only the pre-existing START_RING; pe_truncation 174/174 in
both dirs; macro_order_gate only the known 3 new / 3 stale. Two adversarial review rounds, all findings fixed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
